<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfonso de Molina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1202–1272</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Alfonso of León, Lord of Molina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfonso de Molina was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-ix-of-leon">Alfonso IX of León</a> and brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-of-castile">Ferdinand III of Castile</a>. Through his marriage to the heiress Mafalda he became lord of Molina, tying the semi-independent lordship to the Castilian royal family. His daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-de-molina">María de Molina</a> became queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, and the lordship later passed to the crown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfonso-de-molina.jpg" alt="Alfonso de Molina" width="172" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alonso de Cartagena · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alfonso_de_Molina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
